\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces The four windows containing a spatially significant hit, and the evidence that dispositioned each. $T_\star $ is the search statistic at the stellar position (Eq.\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {eq:tstar}) and `ring max' the largest of the 512 control statistics of the same window; $p$ is the add-one rank probability, whose floor is $1/513=0.0019$. The velocity offset is topocentric, from the nearest catalogued transition of the eight masked species; the $\pm 50$\,km\,s$^{-1}$ mask is applied in the stellar frame after the conversion chain of Appendix\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {app:conventions}. No disposition rests on a single test.}}{9}{table.5}\protected@file@percent }
