\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces 95 per cent upper limits on the fraction $f$ of systems hosting a transmitter above EIRP $P$, from $\DOTSB \prod@ \slimits@ _i(1-f D C_i)=0.05$. Curve (b) is the result of this paper, the injection-measured recovery integrated over each system's fine-channel bandwidth; curves (a) and (c) assume unit recovery and are bracketing calculations only. The shaded region is where the surviving systems cannot exclude $f=1$ and no bound exists, and it grows to cover every $P$ as $D\rightarrow 0$.}}{18}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:occduty}{{8}{18}{95 per cent upper limits on the fraction $f$ of systems hosting a transmitter above EIRP $P$, from $\prod _i(1-f D C_i)=0.05$. Curve (b) is the result of this paper, the injection-measured recovery integrated over each system's fine-channel bandwidth; curves (a) and (c) assume unit recovery and are bracketing calculations only. The shaded region is where the surviving systems cannot exclude $f=1$ and no bound exists, and it grows to cover every $P$ as $D\rightarrow 0$}{figure.8}{}}
